   "edition": "2019",
   "title": "Gap between a protective structure and the floor",
   "paraphrase": "A gap under a guard that bounds a hazard zone must not let a whole body through: at most 180 mm for a slot-shaped gap (the usual floor gap) and 240 mm for a square or round opening. Larger gaps count as whole-body access, not as a lower-limb opening of Table 7.",
